WEBVTT

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.730
So you're asking me whether or not she's Kusakabe Yuka,

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.930
boy?

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.080
The answer is...

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.450
The answer is?

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.700
Yes and no!

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.830
So which is it?

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.100
Yuka-tan?

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.460
You're Yuka-tan, right?

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.460
Kinoshita-san, did you work in the
entertainment industry by any chance?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.080
Not really.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.890
Is there a reason you came to Nourin High?

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.800
Not really.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.700
It's true that she,

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.690
Kinoshita Ringo-san,

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.010
worked in the entertainment industry under the name Kusakabe Yuka.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.220
I knew it!

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.350
But now,

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:46.310
she's left that name behind and
come to us as just another student.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.440
In essence, we're not
to mention her past.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.460
Precisely.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.300
However...

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.070
it'd be <i>so</i> sweet if you three could help her catch up with the rest of the class.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.580
But wait, why us?

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.540
'Cause Kinoshita-san's gonna
be living in the dorms.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.160
What?

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.710
She's even in the same class and program!

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:11.370
Becky's own genius astounds her!

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.600
S-So wait,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.170
y-you're telling me...

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.180
at school, in our dorm, during class, after class, in study hall,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.180
<i>all day</i> I get to be with Yuka-tan?!

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.400
Is that right?

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.410
Yep!

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.220
<i>This must be Heaven!</i>

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:05.240
N-N-Nice to meet you, Yuka-ta—
Kinoshita Ringo-san!

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.740
I am a boy with name is Hata Kousaku.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.730
This is "Young Master",

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:14.190
which is says "Waka Danna" in Japanese.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:19.800
All of us are very enjoying
the study at this school!

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.350
Why does he sound
like Google Translate?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.260
Reckon he's tryin'
to seem "worldly".

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.720
Without further ado, on with the tour!

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.930
This is the main building.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.440
We're divided into classes based on our department.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:36.900
This is the gymnasium.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.340
Behind it are the IP buildings.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.990
Oh, IP stand for industrial promotion.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.700
That's Green Shop Tamo-Nou.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.160
It's where we sell products
we make at school.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.160
I know.

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.020
You know?

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.340
Cats?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.880
Oh, those are peacocks.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:06.510
Plain.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.750
N-No kidding!

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.020
The colorful peacocks you're thinking of are the males.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.640
The females are actually pretty boring.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:19.940
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.320
<i>Is Yuka-tan tired or something?</i>

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.990
This is the wallaby house.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.860
Young Master lives here.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.840
Outfitted with a heated
carpet and air conditioner!

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.190
To be honest, it's fancier than our dorm.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.310
Wallabies are kangaroos?

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.920
Well, they're like cousins, to put it simply.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.250
Um, hey. Uh...

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.260
Let me tell you the sweet, heart-warming story of Young Master and me.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.260
At first, Young Master wasn't
that friendly with us.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.470
But last Christmas, in the chill of night,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:55.560
Young Master escaped from the house and wandered around campus,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.710
Young Master escaped from the house and wandered around campus,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.490
before falling victim to
the cold and collapsing.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.800
But as luck would have it,
I found him lying there

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.660
and brought him back to my room.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:16.080
That night, we slept together,
snuggled inside my body pillow cover.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.590
Since then, Young Master visits us
in the dorm whenever he gets lonely.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:24.300
And we lived happily ever after.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:29.970
M-Moving along!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.680
You're in luck!

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:36.140
This is the finest quality free-range chicken that will ever grace your lips.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.820
Perhaps you know the
big three free-range breeds:

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:41.720
the Hinai Free-range, the Nagoya Cochin, and the Satsuma Native Fowl.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.000
But here in Gifu, we have a breed that
rivals or surpasses them!

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.610
The breed whose meat you hold, the Okumino Free-range!

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.120
Yeah, yeah. Much obliged!

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.080
Thank you, Yoshida.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.030
Nyo nyeed to twank me!

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.790
I-I dwoubt you'll weven twaste the diffwence!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.450
S-So just eat it wiff gwatwitude!

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.550
And nyot to me!

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:02.030
To the thicken, of courthe!

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.460
This girl is abnormal.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.500
H-Hwow ware you!

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.440
B-Beshides, Kamatwowi Kei m-means <i>nyothing</i> nyu me!

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.340
W-Well, he doden't mean nyothing but...

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.640
I-I onwy shee him ash a rival!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.040
By the way, you got eggs here?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:19.850
But of course.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.310
On that note,

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.140
they sell eggs both
fertilized and unfertilized.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.730
Is it true that fertilized eggs
are more nutritious?

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.570
Imbecile!

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.450
You dare even <i>claim</i> to be
an agriculture student?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.220
There's no difference in
inherent nutritional value.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.070
However, eggs farmed
from hens in cramped cages

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:40.200
obviously taste inferior to those laid by hens raised free-range

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.920
and allowed to mingle with roosters.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.070
My apologies.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.130
Hey.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.090
What does "unfertilized egg" mean?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.300
I haven't understood any of
this conversation so far.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.100
Oh, well, it's, you know...

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.310
All this talking is boring.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.600
<i>Th-Th-That's so cute!</i>

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.480
So what are "unfertilized eggs"?

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:04.730
Please hold.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.760
H-Help me out here, Yoshida-san!

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.390
How do I explain this?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.670
What do you need my help for?

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.520
Just explain it like it is.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.940
To a pure, innocent young lady like her?

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:16.720
The carnal details could traumatize her!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.840
Don't be stupid! Haven't you heard of a euphemism?

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.500
You know, like the birds and the bees!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.240
Use your brain for once, plebeian!

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:26.150
Then <i>you</i> explain the difference to her!

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.170
Very well!

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.240
Listen up, newbie!

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.270
Yes?

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.810
I'll answer your question.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.180
Unfertilized eggs...

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:33.390
<i>Gulp...</i>

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.850
...are the eggs you get
when you use a rubber!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.060
Keeping good records is
fundamental to agriculture.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.310
Especially how much of what you planted.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:45.310
Damn Torpedo Tits.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.820
It's vital to keep that straight.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.810
She <i>had</i> to mention rubbers.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.700
By the way, Kinoshita-san,
have you heard of hairy palms?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.650
Like a monkey.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.110
No, no.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.070
The legendary hairy palms that lonely gentlemen get!

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.870
The takeaway is that you
shouldn't overdo anything.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:05.250
It's best to thrust your seed into a new field now and then!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.060
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.800
Wh-What sort of "lesson"
do you think you're teaching here?!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.540
A lesson on crop rotation. Why?

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.560
Crop rotation?

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.220
If you repeatedly plant the
same crop in the same area,

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.880
it'll become prone to sickness and eventually stop growing.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:22.770
Do you understand?

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.420
Hai, wakarimashita!

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:28.230
These lessons are most valuable!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.190
As RA, I would like to make a toast.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:34.070
We have the pleasure this fine day

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.280
of welcoming Kinoshita Ringo-san to our dorm,

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.540
Cheers!

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.540
so let's not stand on ceremony and—

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.160
<i>Listen</i> to me!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.370
Go on, chow down!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.090
It ain't the fanciest party on account of bein' out in the sticks,

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.000
but if there's anythin' we got, it's food!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.020
I can't eat this much.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.360
Honest, what's with
Kinoshita-san's attitude?

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:54.800
Ergh...

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.110
I'm sure she's just nervous.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.420
She must be wary of new people.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:01.560
Then how come she'll talk to <i>you</i> without encouragement?

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.280
You noticed too?

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:05.020
Numskull!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.430
A gal that uppity ain't gonna
get along with no one.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.270
At the end of the day,
farmin's about teamwork.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.490
Point.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.830
Kousaku, don't just go
floatin' away on cloud nine.

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:19.550
Make an effort to build
a relationship with her.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.450
I get it!

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.510
I get it, but...

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.090
A short act for your amusement!

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.790
This is my Fury impression!

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.080
May-lah!

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.390
And now for my second act,

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.170
"Hen Laying Egg"!

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:49.770
Next!

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.240
You nearly cracked it inside me!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:55.820
Shut up!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.530
L-Let's play a game!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.800
K-Kinoshita-san, what game would you'd like to play?

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.680
The King Game.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.460
Who's the King?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.170
It's me!

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.980
<i>I see. Kei's number 1, Minori's 3.</i>

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.850
<i>So number 2...</i>

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:26.350
Number 2 has to feed the King!

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.530
Oh, I'm number 2.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.640
Why are <i>you</i> number 2?!

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:34.650
You're askin' me, numskull!

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:37.900
I signaled that Kinoshita-san
was 3, clear as day.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.330
How was I supposed to get that?!

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:46.210
Stop getting distracted and
play the game, you two.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:48.710
Here.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.730
I feel bashful doin' this in company.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.280
It broke.

00:10:58.210 --> 00:11:00.430
Who's the king?

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:06.390
<i>Checkmate.</i>

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.350
TL note: "doori" means "just according to".

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.350
Plan doori!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.810
N-N-Number 3, step on the
King's face with your bare feet!

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.990
What in tarnation are
you makin' me do?

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:16.810
Twist!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.030
Minori...

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.370
why are <i>you</i> number 3?!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:26.580
Well you done fouled up last time, so I signaled <i>my</i> number this time.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.040
Screw it! Just step on me
and get it over with!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.250
Y-You don't mind, honest?

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:34.710
Well, then...

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.160
Hurry it up.

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:49.190
So this is how you get yer kicks?

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:52.070
You're a right pervert, you are.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.160
A pervert he is not!

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.230
Wheat grows bigger when stomped on!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.150
Men are the same. They get bigger the more you step on them!

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.080
I'm pretty sure that's a perv.

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.400
Not at all!

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.650
N-N-Now see here, Kinoshita-san.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.990
Th-This was just...

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:06.910
It broke.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.410
Who's the king?

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.120
Me.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.400
Golly.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.430
Oh man.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:16.130
Get ready.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.100
Wh-What is it?

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:21.710
Nothing.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:24.470
What number?

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.720
What number?

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.300
It defeats the purpose if I tell you my...

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:30.580
<i>What number?</i>

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.060
N-Number 1.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:41.320
Number 1 must address the King by name.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.940
By name?

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:46.820
So, Ringo-san?

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.530
Just Ringo.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.740
That... directly?

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:52.210
Yes.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.600
And permanently.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.890
Ring—No, Yuka-tan.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.670
Huh? Kinoshita-san?!

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.160
Hey, morning Young Master.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.650
It's Sunday, so we can take it easy all day.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:22.640
But man, get this.

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:25.410
I had this crazy wish-fulfillment dream

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.990
where Yuka-tan transfered
under the name Ringo—

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:35.330
What?

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:37.380
Oh, nothing, nothing!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.270
Thought I was in Inception for a sec!

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:40.650
Anywho, what were you up to?

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.250
Laundry.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.030
Laundry?

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:49.710
What?

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.300
Oh, nothing, just...

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:59.630
Are you perhaps having trouble working the washing machine?

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:00.520
Is that it?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.250
No, it isn't...

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.530
I'm not.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.530
How's laundry done, then?

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:10.860
River.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:13.390
Laundry is done in the river.

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:14.500
I see!

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.750
Like the old lady did in
the Momotaro fairy tale!

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:19.740
But not anymore!

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:23.160
We modern folk use this device!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:29.550
First sort the laundry into colors and whites, cottons and silks.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.670
It's laundry time!

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:32.430
All right!

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.090
Um, Kinoshita-san...

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.980
You don't mind laying out your laundry in front of me?

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:45.050
Why would I?

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.870
'Cause, you know, I'm a guy.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.560
Well, as long as you're okay with it.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.660
What does this go with?

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.040
Oh, panties?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.520
Are those panties cotton or—

00:14:58.020 --> 00:14:59.390
Panties?!

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.850
Th-Those...

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.000
Those...

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:04.880
These...?

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.040
...must be scrubbed by hand.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.000
Scrubbed?

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:08.890
That's right.

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.920
Panties are very delicate, you see.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:14.040
I'm not sure a beginner
like you can handle them.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.350
I see...

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:19.270
S-S-So just this once, I'll do you a favor

